@startuml player_movement_input

package player {
  class Player {
    -- Fields (movement / input) --
    - moving: boolean
    - attemptedMoveThisFrame: boolean
    - lastAttemptStepX: int
    - lastAttemptStepY: int
    - talkNpcIndex: int
    - pickupCooldown: int
    - holding: boolean
    - state: PlayerState
    - lastSnapTimeMs: long

    -- Methods (movement / input) --
    + processInput(): void
    + updateMovement(): void
    + resolveTileOverlapWithPush(stepX:int, stepY:int): boolean
    + snapToTileEdge(dir:String, stepX:int, stepY:int): boolean
    + attemptUnstuck(): boolean
    + recordSafePosition(): void
    + isBlockingLeft(): boolean
    + isGuarding(): boolean
    + startBlockingLeft(): void
    + getDirection(): String
    + setDirection(dir:String): void
    + getSpeed(): int
    + setCollision(flag:boolean): void
    + isCollision(): boolean
    + setWorldX(x:int): void
    + setWorldY(y:int): void
    + getWorldX(): int
    + getWorldY(): int
  }
}

package window {
  class GameWindow {
    + getKeyHandler(): KeyHandler
    + getCollisionChecker(): CollisionChecker
    + getNPC(): Entity[]
    + getObj(): Entity[]
    + getMonster(): Entity[]
    + getItile(): Entity[]
  }
}

package collision {
  class CollisionChecker {
    + checkTile(p:Player, stepX:int, stepY:int): boolean
    + checkEntity(p:Player, list:Entity[], stepX:int, stepY:int): int
  }
}

package key {
  class KeyHandler {
    + isPlayerUp(): boolean
    + isPlayerDown(): boolean
    + isPlayerLeft(): boolean
    + isPlayerRight(): boolean
    + isThrowKeyPressed(): boolean
    + consumeThrowOnce(): void
  }
}

package object {
  class ObjRock {
    + isPickable(): boolean
    + isThrown(): boolean
    + getAlive(): boolean
    + setPickable(b:boolean): void
  }
  class ObjPot {
    + isPickable(): boolean
    + isThrown(): boolean
    + getAlive(): boolean
    + setPickable(b:boolean): void
  }
}

package npc {
  class NpcChicken {
    + isThrown(): boolean
    + isPickable(): boolean
    + getAlive(): boolean
    + onPickedUp(p:Player): void
  }
}

package frame {
  class FrameApp {
    + getTileSize(): int
  }
}

package entity {
  abstract class Entity {
    + isBlocking(): boolean
    + getBounds(): Rectangle2D
  }
}

Player --> window.GameWindow : uses
Player --> collision.CollisionChecker : uses
Player --> key.KeyHandler : uses
Player --> object.ObjRock : may interact
Player --> object.ObjPot : may interact
Player --> npc.NpcChicken : may interact
Player --> frame.FrameApp : reads tile size
CollisionChecker --> Entity : checks [0..*]

note right of Player
**Notes**
- processInput は方向キーの入力を読み取り、向きと moving フラグを設定する。移動キーが押されていない場合は左側ガード（left-blocking）を開始することがある。
- updateMovement は移動を複数ステップに分割して処理し、タイル／エンティティの衝突判定を行い、押し出し（push）・スナップ（snap）・アンストック（unstuck）といった対処を試み、NPC／オブジェクト／モンスターとの相互作用を扱い、
- 衝突がなければ最終的にワールド座標を更新する。

- processInput reads directional keys and sets direction + moving flag; if no movement keys, it may start left-blocking.
- updateMovement splits movement into steps, runs tile/entity collision checks, attempts push/snap/unstuck strategies, handles NPC/OBJ/Monster interactions, and applies final world position updates when no collision.
end note
@enduml